{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF (written HERE because session log 558e-55ce-d9f1-4fa9 is WRITE-BLOCKED) ===\n\nNOTE FOR THE NEXT SESSION: three attempts to append to session log 558e failed with\n'flock: could not acquire lock after 60s', while a probe comment to another ticket landed\nINSTANTLY in the same minute. So the block is SPECIFIC TO 558e, not store-wide contention.\n558e now holds 26 large comments (~160KB); suspect a per-ticket lock or the session-log\nauto-rotation boundary. READ 558e's HANDOFF #22 FIRST, then this. Consider rotating to a new\nsession log rather than fighting it.\n\n=== HANDOFF #22 ADDENDUM — state after the incident, and the two changes now in review ===\n\nBOTH INCIDENT CHANGES ARE ON MAIN. Revert **1292** merged; the evidence-gated re-land **1296**\n(`25ead49f3e`) merged. `reconcile-bridge` is ACTIVE again. Verified empirically: **ZERO\nreconciler-authored `parent_id:\"\"` EDITs after the incident window** (swept the whole tickets branch).\nStore repair is closed out — 61 closed victims accepted by operator ruling, and the two non-closed ones\nrepaired and verified (437c -> 9594, bf03 -> 4804).\n\n--- OPERATOR RULINGS APPLIED THIS STRETCH ---\n * **39c1 is now a CHILD of e369** (operator: \"it should be parented under the epic, which will prevent\n   the epic closing until it is resolved. No separate blocking link is required.\"). Done; e369 cannot\n   close until 39c1 resolves.\n * **2b16: research first, build if a parity gap, defer if not commonly handled.** Researched and\n   recorded with sources on the ticket. **NOT commonly handled** — Aha! refuses deletion propagation\n   outright citing inadvertent-data-loss risk; Asana<->Jira and Workfront<->Jira leave the far item in\n   place; Exalate makes link sync opt-in scripted config. Nor is it a Cloud/DC parity gap (shared core;\n   Cloud never mirrored a peer deletion and has no equivalent cell). **=> DEFERRED**, ACs amended on the\n   ticket, live cell xfail'd with the full reason (change 1303).\n * The dedicated `parent` verb with `--force` is an IDEA, out of scope: `5992-f317-e05e-42f7`.\n * `binding_store` split filed as `4522-e600-9e2c-4823` (it is at 787/800).\n\n--- IN REVIEW RIGHT NOW ---\n  **1302** — 39c1: carry an epic parent to DC via the EPIC LINK. Apply-side ONLY, so bug 8b25's emit\n    gate is untouched and its Cloud guard tests pass UNEDITED (that is the AC satisfied by construction).\n    RED-first: the trio failed on the real `NotImplementedError`, and the overlap cell localised the\n    defect by getting PAST the emit assertion before failing on apply. **Also fixes a second half that\n    would have made it dead on arrival: `build_client_from_settings` now sets\n    `agile_rest_path=\"greenhopper\"`** — without it `add_issues_to_epic` targets the `agile` path DC does\n    not expose. 2047 passed / 1 xfailed, no regressions; transport 780/800.\n  **1303** — 2b16: xfail the live cell with the reason. `strict=False`, so it fails LOUDLY as an xpass\n    if a removal path ever starts working; NOT inverted, NOT deleted.\n\n--- THE OPEN PLATFORM UNKNOWN ON 1302, AND IT IS THE ARBITER ---\nWhether `add_issues_to_epic` succeeds against DC 8.17.1 is NOT established from documentation.\npycontribs routes it to `{agile_rest_path}/1.0/epics/{epic}/add`, and some DC versions key that by epic\n**ID** rather than KEY. The greenhopper sentinel epic `\"none\"` is used to express a CLEAR. If the live\ncell fails on either point, the documented fallback is a direct write of the instance-discovered\n`Epic Link` `customfield_NNNNN`. **Do not conclude the fix works off the unit suite** — that is the\nexact mistake 2b16's change 1276 made.\n\n--- HARNESS ---\nRun **30834117797** dispatched on `25ead49f3e` (i.e. WITH 1296). It is the run that arbitrates 88d9's\nlive cell and refreshes 5200's cell verdicts. **The earlier run 30828166841 is UNUSABLE — it ran the\nDEFECTIVE main (`6baa030460`); its verdicts were deliberately never read.** After 1302/1303 land, ONE\nmore run is needed so the suite reflects the epic-link path and the xfail.\nREMINDER, paid for twice: after a Gerrit submit, `git fetch origin main` and confirm your commit is on\nthe MIRROR before dispatching a workflow on `main`.\n\n--- WHAT REMAINS FOR e369 ---\n 1. land 1302 + 1303.\n 2. one final harness run; read per-cell verdicts AND the `collected=N executed=N skipped=0` line.\n 3. close 88d9 (`--class preexisting`; its AC accepts GREEN **or** the `SETUP FAILED` platform branch —\n    DC refuses to null a sub-task's `fields.parent`, HTTP 400 \"data was not an object\").\n 4. close 2b16 (amended ACs recorded), close 39c1, close 5200 (18 ACs already verified — it waits only\n    on the run).\n 5. **re-run e369's plan review LAST** (`stale-code`), then close e369."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785776891403147001,"uuid":"208adbc8-f1d7-4439-9b69-836343de8dbd"}